p ALL ccr/cx logic: multi-root transcript discovery (native + CCR profile mirrors), is_ccr_path checks, cx attribution to the Codex plan, catalog-based context windows, and every test fixture that builds .claude-code-router trees. Report exactly what a stock version looks like (single ~/.claude/projects root, claude attribution only) and which functions/tests to delete vs simplify. Line references.\n2. herdr/crates/usage-dash-core/src/sources/codex.rs — ccr-model-catalog.json usage (~/.codex/ccr-model-catalog.json): is the catalog ONLY for cx sessions or does codex itself need it? Determine whether removal breaks stock codex context-window display; report the stock fallback.\n3. herdr/crates/usage-dash-model, goal-dash-core (context.rs, timegate.rs) — the /Users/ hits look like test fixtures; confirm each is harmless test data vs real logic.\n4. herdr/src/harness_host.rs — the harness/dash host: \"cx\" orchestrator kind, ccp profile source, ~/claude-hub paths (lines ~178, 938, 1003, 1135-1149, 2788). Map the full ccp \"profile source\" feature (state.rs disable/enable entry + profile source) and what removal implies for harness-manager-ui plugin.\n5. herdr-plugins repo: agent-launcher (tui/src/main.rs mentions /Users default carry-over), claude-image-preview, plugin-manager — grep for cx/ccr/ccp AND hardcoded paths (/Users/, /home/andual, /opt/homebrew, .bun/bin absolute, keychain, osascript, mac binaries). Report each with file:line and whether it breaks portability.\n6. herdr-mirror repo: same grep; the /Users/n/proj hits look like tests — confirm. Also check its config defaults for mac assumptions.\n7. Machine-wide hardcode sweep across ALL THREE repos (excluding target/): grep -rn for '/Users/', '/home/andual', '/opt/homebrew', 'Library/Application Support', 'osascript', 'pbcopy', 'pbpaste', 'security find', '\\.bun/bin', '/usr/local/bin', 'andual' in source (rs, toml, ts, sh, go, json — NOT lockfiles). Classify each hit: test fixture (harmless) / comment / real